Hey Mike! Did endoR ever get linked to the DEB model in the same way as the ectotherm model as you described in this thread? I've been asked to work on some thermal/mechanistic distribution models for a bird that happens to have parameters in the Add My Pet database, so having access to the full bird model DEB linked with microclimate responses would be awesome. But the endoR in the NicheMapR version I just re-downloaded still doesn't seem to have that option. Figured I'd ask on this thread, since a lot of time has passed since I asked the original question!

Best
Adam

On Wednesday, March 10, 2021 at 3:07:30 PM UTC-5 Michael Kearney wrote:
> Hi Adam,
>
> Not quite but that is a priority for this year. Marko Jusup and I are refining exactly how to compute heat production from the DEB model and will then finalise a whole-life-cycle bird model. For mammals we also need to integrate a variant of the standard DEB model that includes lactation, which was largely worked out in collaboration with Bas Kooijman during Jess Roberts' PhD work. Also the software note for the endoR model is still in review but that will hopefully appear by the middle of the year.
>
> All the best,
> Mike
>
> On Thursday, March 11, 2021 at 4:08:09 AM UTC+11 aeic...@gmail.com wrote:
> > Hey Mike! Just wanted to ask whether the endotherm model in R is ready to be linked to the DEB processes in the same way as the ectotherm model. I wasn't sure if it's at the point where I can do Dynamic Energy Budgets of mammals yet.
> >
> > Thank you!
> > Adam

